{"config_json": "{
  "record_grain": "licence_or_permit",
  "grain_rationale": "One record is one QBCC licence (licence number, grade/class and financial category, held by a licensee). The business participant is the licensee, so the record's own Licence Number is the licence identifier and is explicitly NOT mapped as a business identifier. A licensee may hold several licences, so holder attributes repeat across records and record_id is the datastore row id, not the licence.",
  "reader": {"format": "json", "archive_member": null, "encoding": "utf-8-sig", "delimiter": null, "skip_rows": 0, "sheet": null, "record_path": "result.records"},
  "record_id": {"strategy": "columns", "source_paths": ["_id"], "rationale": "Datastore _id is present on 100% of rows and 508/508 distinct in discovery. Licence Number has only 506 distinct over 508 rows (duplicate licence numbers), so it is not unique per record; _id is."},
  "observed_at": {"source_path": null, "steps": [], "fallback": "resource_last_modified"},
  "fields": [
    {"source_paths": ["Licensee Name"], "join_with": " ", "target": "entity.legal_name", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": "current_legal_name", "steps": [{"op": "trim"}, {"op": "collapse_whitespace"}], "confidence": 0.85, "rationale": "Header 'Licensee Name' = holder of the QBCC licence; a licence is issued to a legal person, so this is the holder's legal name. Publisher evidence confirms a licence may be held by an individual or a company. Values are person names in caps or company names ending PTY LTD, consistent with registered names rather than trading names."},
    {"source_paths": ["ABN"], "join_with": "", "target": "entity.abn", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": null, "steps": [{"op": "abn"}], "confidence": 0.92, "rationale": "Column labelled ABN, 54.9% present, shape '99 999 999 999', checksum-valid rate 0.996. Publisher: ABN is issued separately for tax and trading and is collected on the application, so it identifies the holder's business. The abn transform rejects the ~0.4% bad checksums rather than guessing."},
    {"source_paths": ["ACN"], "join_with": "", "target": "entity.acn", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": null, "steps": [{"op": "acn"}], "confidence": 0.92, "rationale": "Column labelled ACN, shape '999 999 999', 100% checksum-valid on the 6.7% of rows present. Collected on the company application per publisher evidence; populated on exactly the 34 Company rows. Taken from its own column only, never derived from ABN."},
    {"source_paths": ["Licence Type DESC"], "join_with": "", "target": "entity.entity_type", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": null, "steps": [{"op": "map_enum", "args": {"mapping": {"Company": "company"}, "default": "unknown", "passthrough": false}}], "confidence": 0.6, "rationale": "Only 'Company' reliably states legal form, and it agrees with ACN being populated on the same 34 rows. 'Individual' is deliberately mapped to unknown: an individual licensee may be a sole trader, a partner, or an individual nominee for a company, and the publisher states a licence category does not establish the holder's legal form."},
    {"source_paths": ["Licensee Business Address"], "join_with": "", "target": "address.full", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": "licence_holder_address", "steps": [{"op": "trim"}, {"op": "collapse_whitespace"}], "confidence": 0.8, "rationale": "Publisher: the application collects the licensee's business address and it is published in the licence register. One free-text line of street, locality, state and postcode. Scope is licence_holder_address, not registered office or licensed premises."},
    {"source_paths": ["Licensee Business Address"], "join_with": "", "target": "address.state", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": "licence_holder_address", "steps": [{"op": "regex_extract", "args": {"pattern": "\\b(NSW|VIC|QLD|WA|SA|TAS|ACT|NT)\\b", "group": 1}}, {"op": "state"}], "confidence": 0.82, "rationale": "State abbreviation sits in the address line just before the 4-digit postcode. Extracted by state transform from its own evidence; not assumed to be QLD although most rows are."},
    {"source_paths": ["Licensee Business Address"], "join_with": "", "target": "address.postcode", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": "licence_holder_address", "steps": [{"op": "regex_extract", "args": {"pattern": "(\\d{4})\\s*$", "group": 1}}, {"op": "postcode"}], "confidence": 0.8, "rationale": "Address lines end with a 4-digit postcode; pattern anchored at end of string so street numbers are not matched."},
    {"source_paths": ["Licensee Business Address"], "join_with": "", "target": "address.locality", "when": null, "valid_from_path": null, "valid_to_path": null, "validity_date_formats": [], "claim_scope": "licence_holder_address", "steps": [{"op": "regex_extract", "args": {"pattern": "\\s([^,]+?)\\s+(?:NSW|VIC|QLD|WA|SA|TAS|ACT|NT)\\s+\\d{4}\\s*$", "group": 1}}, {"op": "trim"}], "confidence": 0.6, "rationale": "Locality is the text between street and state abbreviation. The address is unstructured free text with inconsistent casing and no street/suburb delimiter, so the split is heuristic and can mis-split when a street name ends in a locality-like token."}
  ],
  "constants": [
    {"target": "address.country", "value": "AU", "confidence": 0.85, "rationale": "Queensland (Australia) licensing register; all sampled addresses carry an Australian state abbreviation and 4-digit postcode."}
  ],
  "unmapped": [
    {"source_path": "_id", "reason": "Datastore row identifier used only as record_id; it is an API artefact, not a business identifier."},
    {"source_path": "Licence Number", "reason": "Identifier of the licence, not of the business. Per mapping rules the record's own ID must not be mapped as a business identifier. Non-unique across rows (506/508) and not an ABN/ACN, so no ontology target applies."},
    {"source_path": "Licence Type CODE", "reason": "Redundant coded form of Licence Type DESC ('I'/'C'); same semantic, already used via the DESC column. No separate target."},
    {"source_path": "Financial Category DESC", "reason": "Financial/financial-category status of the licence (single value 'Self Certification - Trade' in discovery). This is a licence attribute, not entity.status; ontology has no licence-status field."},
    {"source_path": "Financial Category CODE", "reason": "Coded form of Financial Category DESC; licence attribute, no ontology target."},
    {"source_path": "Licence Grade", "reason": "Grade/type of the licence (e.g. Trade Contractor Licence, Site Supervisor). A licence attribute, not the holder's business form, so it must not feed entity_type. No ontology field for licence grade."},
    {"source_path": "Licence Class Type", "reason": "Licence class (e.g. Carpentry, Plumbing and Drainage) — the licensed trade. Not an ANZSIC code, and entity.industry_code asks for ANZSIC where available, so mapping it would misstate the coded industry; kept unmapped with the raw values preserved in source."}
  ],
  "notes": "Despite advertised_format CSV, the file is a data.gov.au CKAN/DataStore API JSON envelope with the rows under result.records (magic 7b2268656c70223a = '{\"help\":'). Reader therefore uses format json with record_path 'result.records'. record_grain is licence_or_permit: the holder's attributes (name, ABN/ACN, address, entity_type) are repeated once per licence held, which is why names/locations have duplicate-ish distinct counts. Publisher evidence was used for entity_type caution and for the business-address semantics. Observed_at falls back to resource_last_modified because no date column exists in the register extract."
}"}
